  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 101 PM CDT Wed Aug 12 2026\n\nThe upper level ridge will continue to shift westward Friday into \nthe weekend, with the ribbon of mid/upper level moisture responsible \nfor Wed-Thu storm chances consequently retreating back towards the \nFour Corners. Thunderstorm potential will therefore decrease, \nalthough a few isolated storms may still develop near the TX/NM \nstate line through Friday evening. Dry weather is favored to return \nto the entire forecast area Sat-Sun and into at least early next \nweek as ridging aloft continues to build overhead. Temperatures will \nremain about 5 degrees above normal for this time of year this \nweekend through next week, with little signal for any meaningful \ncooldown or precipitation chances through the end of the extended \nforecast period.",
